    "result": "I fixed it in `status.go`, but I could not run the tests because the permission prompt for `go test` was declined.\n\nThe bug: all jobs shared `status.json`, and each `Report` read the file, changed it and wrote it back. When two jobs did this at the same time, the later write erased the other job's update. A dashboard read during a write could also get a half-written file.\n\nThe change:\n- Each job now writes only its own file, `status.d/\u003chex of job name\u003e`. It writes a temporary file and then renames it into place, so a reader never sees a partial status.\n- `Statuses` reads all the job files and merges them. It also still reads the old `status.json`, so jobs that reported before this change still show.\n- On Windows the rename fails while the dashboard has the file open, so it retries for up to 0.5 s.\n- A job must report from only one process at a time. That is now a comment in the code, not something the code enforces.\n\nNew file: `status_test.go`. It starts 20 separate processes that report at once, and it checks the old-file fallback. Run `go test ./...` to check it.",
